From 50e6d30dc4d6fe590731023f351ecb1e0c8db833 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonny Heggheim <hegjon@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:13:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] libalpm: btrpkg: pacman -U of .pkg.btr, -Sp without
 btrpkg, signify not recorded as pgp

- alpm_pkg_load of a btrpkg cache file (pacman -U, -Qp): the .sig is
  signify, checked against the btrpkg keys as LocalFileSigLevel asks,
  never handed to GPGME; with full, every chunk's data is checked
  against the index (only pull-ids checked chunks before, so -U
  installed a damaged file silently). alpm_pkg_check_pgp_signature
  reports no OpenPGP signature for such a file.
- A transaction that only prints (NOLOCK, pacman -Sp) no longer selects
  or plans btrpkg downloads: the stock file names and sizes, no network
  I/O, as root or not (as root it printed a .pkg.btr URL no server has).
- A signify check is recorded as btrpkg-validation=signify:KEY extended
  data and %VALIDATION% keeps sha256 (the ID check), not pgp. A new
  validation token would make the stock pacman beside pacman-btrpkg warn
  on every read of the local database. A btrpkg-validation entry in a
  package's own .PKGINFO is dropped.
